{
 "description": "Shared MAVLink decoder fixture for SatMap's Drone link (iPhone SatMap/Core and android/core). Each case is ONE UDP datagram (hex). 'expect' lists the messages the decoder must emit, in order; [] means nothing is emitted. 'raw' holds MAVLink field values as on the wire (names as in common.xml); 'decoded' holds the SI-friendly values the apps use (degrees, metres, m/s, volts, amperes, percent; null = not available).",
 "generator": "docs/mavlink/make_fixtures.py (pymavlink 2.4.50, common dialect)",
 "tolerance": 1e-06,
 "rules": [
  "Start bytes: 0xFE = MAVLink 1 (6-byte header), 0xFD = MAVLink 2 (10-byte header).",
  "CRC is X.25 (CRC-16/MCRF4XX, init 0xFFFF) over the header without the start byte, the payload as received, then the message's CRC_EXTRA byte; stored little-endian.",
  "MAVLink 2 incompat flag 0x01 = signed: 13 signature bytes follow the CRC; skip them, do not verify. Any other incompat bit: reject the frame.",
  "MAVLink 2 payloads may be shorter than the full length (trailing zeros trimmed): zero-extend before reading fields. MAVLink 1 payloads have no extension fields.",
  "Payload fields are little-endian, in wire order (sorted by type size, extensions last).",
  "Unknown message id or CRC mismatch: drop the start byte and resync one byte on.",
  "A frame that runs past the end of the datagram is dropped.",
  "HEARTBEAT with type 6 (GCS) or autopilot 8 (INVALID) never creates a drone (tracksDrone = false).",
  "Sentinels -> null: GLOBAL_POSITION_INT.hdg 65535; SYS_STATUS voltage 65535, current -1, remaining -1; BATTERY_STATUS remaining -1; GPS_RAW_INT satellites 255.",
  "ADSB_VEHICLE callsign: up to the first NUL, trailing spaces trimmed; empty -> null. icaoHex is 6 upper-case hex digits. altitude_type 0 = pressure (QNH), 1 = geometric. Use heading/velocity/callsign only when the matching 'valid' flag is set."
 ],
 "messages": {
  "0": {
   "name": "HEARTBEAT",
   "crcExtra": 50,
   "v1Length": 9,
